course: dictionary
lesson: 276
title: Ambushers: waiting to strike
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ambusher is a person or animal that hides and waits to attack someone by surprise. The word comes from ambush, a surprise attack from a hiding place. An ambush is the trick, and an ambusher is the one who does it.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence: «the python and the praying mantis are the patient ambushers». Patient means able to wait calmly for a long time. A python does not chase its dinner. It waits, still and hidden, until the prey comes close, then it strikes.
explain: Writers use this word to compare animals. «The sparrowhawk is a hedge-hopping ambusher» tells you the sparrowhawk flies low along hedges to surprise its prey. Test your meaning: swap in "an animal that hides and waits to attack". If the sentence still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: An ambusher is a person or animal that hides and waits to attack someone by surprise.
fact: «Ambusher» is a noun. The plural is «ambushers».
fact: Crocodiles and some spiders are ambushers: they wait for their prey to come close.
fact: «Patient» means able to wait calmly for a long time, so patient ambushers wait before they strike.
fact: «Hedge-hopping» means flying low over hedges.
exercise: «The python is one of the patient ambushers.» What is an ambusher? | A fish that swims in the open sea | A bird that sings at dawn | A runner that chases its prey for miles | *A person or animal that hides and waits to attack by surprise
exercise: «The sparrowhawk is a hedge-hopping ambusher.» What does hedge-hopping mean? | *Flying low over hedges | Hopping on the ground | Singing from the top of a tree | Swimming under water
exercise: Find and copy the one word that names an animal that hides and waits to surprise its prey. | missile | sprinter | hook | *ambusher
test: «The crocodile lay still in the mud, waiting for a deer to come down to the river.» What is the crocodile in this sentence? | A sprinter that runs faster than any other animal | A fishing hook | *An ambusher, waiting to strike by surprise | A flying clean-up crew
test: Which swap best checks the meaning of ambusher in «the praying mantis is a patient ambusher»? | A fast runner that chases its prey | *Someone who hides and waits to attack by surprise | A fish that swims in circles | A bird that sings loudly at dawn
exam: «The spider sits still in its web, and waits for an insect to land.» Which word from this lesson describes the spider? | A missile | A sprinter | A flying clean-up crew | *An ambusher
